{"title":"Career Roadmap: Fisheries Officer","role":"Fisheries Officer","summary":"A Fisheries Officer works in the management, development, conservation and sustainable utilization of aquatic resources. Depending on the employer, responsibilities can include:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc. (Bachelor of Science – General / Honours)","Course":"Zoology"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build expertise in aquatic biology, fisheries science, aquaculture, fish health, conservation, fisheries management and field operations"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Fisheries Officer works in the management, development, conservation and sustainable utilization of aquatic resources. Depending on the employer, responsibilities can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fisheries resource assessment"},{"text":"Fish population monitoring"},{"text":"Aquaculture development"},{"text":"Fish health and disease management"},{"text":"Fisher community support"},{"text":"Fisheries regulation and enforcement"},{"text":"Hatchery management"},{"text":"Aquatic ecosystem conservation"},{"text":"Data collection and reporting"},{"text":"Implementation of fisheries-development programs"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A B.Sc. Zoology provides a relevant biological foundation, but eligibility for government Fisheries Officer posts can vary by recruitment notification. Some posts specifically require a degree in Fisheries Science, Aquaculture or a related discipline. Students should verify the exact qualification requirements for each recruitment examination."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof to Create","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"1st Year"},{"text":"Zoology & aquatic biology fundamentals"},{"text":"Animal biology, ecology, evolution"},{"text":"Aquatic biodiversity portfolio"},{"text":"Weak biology fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2nd Year"},{"text":"Fish biology & ecology"},{"text":"Ichthyology, physiology, taxonomy"},{"text":"Fish identification project"},{"text":"Only textbook knowledge"}],[{"text":"3rd Year"},{"text":"Fisheries & aquaculture"},{"text":"Fish culture, breeding, nutrition, disease"},{"text":"Aquaculture project"},{"text":"No practical field exposure"}],[{"text":"Final Year"},{"text":"Fisheries management"},{"text":"Conservation, data, policy, field methods"},{"text":"Fisheries management capstone + internship"},{"text":"No fieldwork"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 1–2 — Biological Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Animal diversity"},{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Evolution"},{"text":"Ecology"},{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Basic chemistry"},{"text":"Environmental science"},{"text":"Statistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop an understanding of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Aquatic ecosystems"},{"text":"Freshwater ecosystems"},{"text":"Marine ecosystems"},{"text":"Food chains"},{"text":"Biodiversity"},{"text":"Population dynamics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 3–4 — Fish Biology"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ichthyology"},{"text":"Fish taxonomy"},{"text":"Fish anatomy"},{"text":"Fish physiology"},{"text":"Fish genetics"},{"text":"Fish reproduction"},{"text":"Fish ecology"},{"text":"Aquatic microbiology"},{"text":"Limnology"},{"text":"Marine biology"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn fish identification using:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Morphological characteristics"},{"text":"Meristic characteristics"},{"text":"Identification keys"},{"text":"Habitat"},{"text":"Feeding behaviour"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semesters 5–6 — Fisheries & Aquaculture"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Capture fisheries"},{"